<code>assert c != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i &amp;&amp; i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert c != null => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>
--------------------
To generate the assert statement for the given comment, we need to ensure that if the collection `c` is not null, then the constructed `ArrayList` is equal to the collection `c`. Since there isn't a direct method to compare the entire list with a collection in the provided API, we can infer that the list should contain all elements of the collection in the same order and have the same size.

Here's the assert statement based on these observations:

<code>assert c != null => this.size() == c.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.size(); this.get(i).equals(c.toArray()[i]);</code>

This assert statement checks:
1. If the collection `c` is not null.
2. The size of the constructed list is equal to the size of the collection.
3. Each element in the constructed list matches the corresponding element in the collection.
